1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
This independent portfolio builds on my clinical operations experience.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:30,000
I do not claim direct MSL or CV experience. This is not an official Bayer tool.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
My morning desk brings together Bayer and cardiovascular news. Hovering over a card reveals a note.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Saved articles and newly retrieved RSS items are labelled separately, with dates and sources.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:15,000
I choose an example, edit the query if needed, and run a real search.

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Papers, trial registries and the basket have separate columns. I expand the documents I need.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Selected documents retain their sources and feed the pre-visit report.

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
I check the HCP name, hospital, specialty and product using public articles.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:15,000
An event appearance does not establish Bayer KOL status. I also check author affiliations.

10
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
After reading the papers and articles, I write the questions I want to explore.

11
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I ask about unresolved issues, such as the burden of testing or applicability of the evidence.

12
00:02:45,000 --> 00:03:00,000
After the visit, I separate questions, observations, interpretation, hypotheses and insight candidates.

13
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:15,000
The recording example is a practice conversation, not the public clinician’s words or an activity result.

14
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:30,000
I review the search terms, retrieve related papers, registries and news, and distinguish abstracts from full text.

15
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:45,000
Charts show selected documents and recorded question topics. Study effects are read within each study’s context.

16
00:03:45,000 --> 00:04:00,000
I can share separate HTML reports before and after the visit, with outstanding review needs retained.
